            <ArticleTitle>[Wünderlich s syndrome: importance of diagnostic imaging].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>917-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Wünderlich's Syndrome is a spontaneous retroperitoneal haemorrhage characterised by sudden lumbar pain, tangible mass in the lumbar region and signs of hypovolaemic shock.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE REPORT" NlmCategory="METHODS">A 65 year-old female presented the classic triad indicating Wünderlich's syndrome. Imaging techniques with three-dimensional reconstruction enabled us to determine the diagnosis and aetiology, and aided in determining the treatment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DISCUSSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">We emphasise the importance of imaging methods in diagnosing and choosing treatment for Wünderlich s Syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
